# kaniko and docker read .dockerignore from the build context root, and the
# backend is its own context (scripts/build-image.sh, and the Jenkins
# helmCharts.kaniko("backend/Dockerfile", "backend", ...) call). A .dockerignore
# at the repository root is never read for this build.
#
# Everything listed here is a path the Dockerfile does not COPY (it takes only
# pyproject.toml, poetry.lock, run.py, alembic.ini, app/ and alembic/), so this
# file cannot change what CI builds — it only stops the dev environment from
# streaming its build and tool output to the builder. CI never noticed the
# absence because it builds from a clean clone; here the lint and test gates
# leave 20M+ of .mypy_cache behind, and the context was 86 MiB without this.
.git
.venv
node_modules
**/__pycache__
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.env
.env.test
tmp
test-app
MagicMock
tests
docs
.claude
